# Implementation Plan — High-Precision Universal Docket Filter

Design and implement an executive-grade, multi-attribute Docket Filter across all 5 hiring pipeline stages (**1. Dossier**, **2. 4-Pillar DSS**, **3. Dept Head Rubric**, **4. HRMPSB Deliberation**, and **5. Appointment Resolution**) to uniquely identify every applicant, resolve duplicate/matching names, and enable instant search by Name, Application ID, Filing Date, or Target Position.

## User Requirements & Problem Analysis
1. **Duplicate / Matching Names**: Multiple applicants may share identical or similar names. The system must display **Full Name + Unique Tracking ID (`NBSC-APP-2026-XXXXX`) + Filing Date (`Aug 20, 2026`) + Vacancy Item** in the selector and pills.
2. **High Applicant Volume**: Evaluators need instant filtering rather than scrolling through dozens or hundreds of entries.
3. **Multi-Attribute Search**: Real-time search by typing any fragment of the applicant's name, tracking ID number, application date, or position.
4. **Consistency**: The filter must be seamlessly synchronized across all 5 pipeline stage pages so moving from Stage 1 to 5 preserves the selected candidate.

